{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GizvCanQEtsPCwn4q9mcgz","type":"tool_result","content":"| 120 | 0.010 (0.36) | 0.017 (0.27) | 0.034 (0.92) | 0.051 (0.92) | 0.100\\* | — | — | — | — |\n\nMedians are within one unit of the means everywhere. At `n = 60` the mean\nnumber of components is 45.6, 30.9, 18.5, 10.7, 4.3, 2.0, 1.1, 1, 1 for the\nnine values of `c`, so the cells `c ≤ 2` are forests-plus-a-few-cycles and\ntheir pathwidth is that of the largest component, which is why `pw/n` there\ntends to 0 (§2).\n\n**Finite-size behaviour, and the test of §1.4 (item 5 of §7(b)).** `pw/n`\nfalls with `n` at every `c`, as Gogate–Dechter's treewidths did. On the cells\nwith at least 12 proved graphs, `pw` is linear in `n` to the eye, and a least\nsquares fit `pw ≈ β_∞ n + γ` gives:\n\n| `c` | `β_∞` (fit) | `γ` | `β*(c)` (§1.4, derived LB) | PS tw LB | best UB (§7(a)) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2 | 0.040 | 1.8 | 0 | 0 | 0.162 |\n| 3 | 0.099 | 2.1 | 0.009 | 0 | 0.260 |\n| 4 | 0.158 | 2.4 | 0.061 | 0 | 0.347 |\n| 6 | 0.268 | 2.6 | 0.171 | 0.092 | 0.520 |\n| 8 | 0.360 | 2.6 | 0.263 | 0.214 | 0.693 |\n| 10 | 0.415 | 3.1 | 0.337 | 0.297 | 0.760 |\n\n---- tests ----\n\"\"\"loop0011 item 02: the deterministic lemmas of the separator first moment\n(`learning.separator_moment`, `reports/separator_moment.md` §2).\n\nL1  a graph of pathwidth `k < n` has an exact-size empty pair (`|A| = ⌈(n − k)/2⌉`,\n    `|R| = ⌊(n − k)/2⌋`);\nL1′ equivalently a `k`-set `S` in `E_bip`; `E_bip ⊆ E_relax`, strictly;\nL2  the alternating closure of any empty pair is monotone, stops after one\n    round, and lands on a closed pair `S* = N(A*) ∩ N(R*)` of the forced sizes;\nL3  on the MOSP graph a pair is empty iff no pattern meets both sides.\n\nEvery labelled graph on ≤ 6 vertices is enumerated here; the full check (every\ngraph to 9 vertices, 20,000 random at 10–12, 2,000 covers) is\n`reports/scratch/separator_moment/02_lemmas/check.py`.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__