titioning","+   `V`, `|A| ≥ t`, `|R| ≥ N − t`, `|S| ≤ k`, no `A–R` edge, every vertex of `S`","+   adjacent to `A` and to `R` (`S = N(A) ∩ N(R)`, §2.3);","+3. the **combined count**: closed pairs grouped by their separator `S*`,","+   `|S*| = s′ ≤ k`. Given `G − S`, the empty bipartitions `(A, R)` with","+   `|A| ∈ [t, t + k − s′]` (so that `|R| ≥ N − t`) are 2-colourings of the","+   components of `G − S`, at most `2^κ` of them (`κ` the number of","+   components), and each is closed with probability","+   `Π_{v∈S} q_{|A|} q_{|R|} ≤ Qmax(s′)^{s′}` (`q_x = 1 − (1 − p)^x`; the edges","+   from `S` to `G − S` are independent of `G − S`, and for distinct `v ∈ S`","+   they are disjoint edge sets). Hence","+","+       P(pw ≤ k) ≤ Σ_{s′ ≤ k} C(n, s′) · Qmax(s′)^{s′} · E_{N′ = n − s′}[ 1[E_win] · 2^κ ],","+","+   with `E_win` the window bipartition event (one side between `t` and","+   `t + k − s′` vertices; `E_bip` at `s′ = k`) or its relaxation (no","+   component larger than `t + k − s′`). The inner factor is a *tilted*","+   partition sum, computed exactly by the recursions of §5.1 with every","+   part weighted by 2 (`tilt = ln 2` in `log_prob_bip` / `log_prob_rel`).","+","+**Size range.** Asymptotic constants (roots of exponents per vertex);","+fitted rates from exact inner sums at `N = 100–400`; the threshold check at","+`N ≤ 400`; the finite form at `n = 60, 120`, `c = 3, 4, 6, 8, 10`, every `k`","+around the floors. Checks on record (`check.log`): the window and tilted","+recursions against the enumeration of every labelled graph at `N ≤ 6`","+(every window, both tilts; max difference `3 × 10⁻¹³`); the fast relaxed","+recursion against the table one at `N ≤ 6` and `N = 60, 120, 200`","+(`6 × 10⁻¹⁴`); the finite closed count against the enumeration of closed","+pairs over every labelled graph at `n ≤ 6` (`3 × 10⁻¹³`) and Monte Carlo","+at `n = 7, 8` (20,000 graphs each: `2.1, 0.8, 0.2` standard errors);","+`β_sep` with the bracket's lower end equals `β*` at six `c